<header class="sp-head"><p class="featured-region">23 March 1775 · Richmond, Virginia</p><h1 class="sp-title">Give Me Liberty or Give Me Death</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patrick-henry">Patrick Henry</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>As tension with Britain rose, the Second Virginia Convention met in a church in Richmond to decide whether to raise a militia. Patrick Henry argued that war was already inevitable and that further petitions were useless.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>Key passage</h2><blockquote class="sp-quote"><p>I know not what course others may take; but as for me, give me liberty or give me death!</p></blockquote><p class="sp-source">As reconstructed by William Wirt in his life of Patrick Henry (1817).</p><div class="sp-full"><a class="sp-full-link" href="https://avalon.law.yale.edu/18th_century/patrick.asp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the complete text<span aria-hidden="true"> &#8599;</span></a><span class="sp-full-src">The Avalon Project, Yale Law School</span></div></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>The convention voted to arm the colony. Within a month fighting broke out at Lexington and Concord, beginning the American Revolutionary War.</p><div class="sp-led"><h3 class="sp-led-k">What it led to</h3><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battles-of-lexington-and-concord">Battles of Lexington and Concord</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-declaration-of-independence">Declaration of Independence</a></div></div></section>
